---
import GameLayout from "../../../layouts/GameLayout.astro";
---

<GameLayout title="OverTheWire: Leviathan" gameName="leviathan">
    <h1 class="text-[30pt] font-normal leading-[1.2em] mb-4">Leviathan</h1>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <em class="block mb-4">
            Leviathan: (noun) a sea monster. (adjective) huge; enormous.
        </em>
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">About Leviathan</h3>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        This wargame doesn't require any knowledge about programming - just a
        bit of common sense and some knowledge about basic *nix commands.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Leviathan's levels are called <strong
            >leviathan0, leviathan1, ... etc.</strong
        > and can be accessed on <strong>leviathan.labs.overthewire.org</strong> through
        SSH on port 2223.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">To login to the first level use:</p>

    <pre
        class="bg-[#F5F5F5] p-4 mb-4 font-mono text-sm border border-[#E3E3E3] overflow-auto">Username: leviathan0
Password: leviathan0</pre>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Data for the levels can be found in <strong>the homedirectories</strong
        >. You can look at <strong>/etc/leviathan_pass</strong> for the various level
        passwords.
    </p>
</GameLayout>
